&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces in Health Care (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast Company Most Innovative Companies (2020, 2023)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces NY (2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is responsible for Maven’s end-to-end benefits and payments platform, including eligibility and enrollments.&amp;nbsp; Maven’s benefits products should be easy to use for members, providers and employers. You will work closely with Engineering and Design teams, as well as with Maven’s Growth and Client Success teams, and with clients.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for someone who has scaled a benefits or complex B2B2C operational product to the point where it runs quietly, and who has the client-facing judgment to decide what gets built, when, and for whom.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you'll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the benefits product end to end: eligibility, enrollment, claims adjudication, payer and employer reconciliation, and provider payments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make it scale and just work: drive the shift from manual to programmatic reconciliation, self-serve eligibility, and automated claims so member and provider volume grows without operational headcount growing with it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and enforce a triage framework for custom client requests: evaluate against platform leverage, sequence against the core roadmap, route to the right owner, and communicate decisions with clarity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and develop a team of PMs spanning benefits, payments, and eligibility/enrollments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
